What is a Load Bank?
Load Banks are specialized electrical devices designed to provide a precisely controlled electrical load for testing power sources such as engine generators, gas turbines, and Uninterruptible Power Supplies (UPS). They are crucial for factory acceptance tests, the commissioning of new power assets, and preventative maintenance to mitigate issues such as "wet stacking" in diesel generators. Essentially, they simulate the real-world electrical demands that a power source would encounter during actual operation. This allows engineers and technicians to validate the performance, capacity, and reliability of these systems under safe, controlled conditions, ensuring they will perform as expected during a real power outage.
